/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The USA, who has the highest corporation tax rate but the middle level of FDI. The level of FDI is influenced by a number of factors and not just the rate of corporation tax. For instance, firms may be attracted by the presence of skilled labour and good infrastructure. To finance a good education system and provision of, for instance, good roads, a government may impose relatively high tax rates. A growing economy may also attract FDI as foreign firms may expect a growing market for their products. Foreign MNCs will be encouraged to set up in countries where they expect to receive high net profit.)
/E (The USA, who has the highest corporation tax rate but the middle level of FDI. The level of FDI is influenced by a number of factors and not just the rate of corporation tax. For instance, firms may be attracted by the presence of skilled labour and good infrastructure. To finance a good education system and provision of, for instance, good roads, a government may impose relatively high tax rates. A growing economy may also attract FDI as foreign firms may expect a growing market for their products. Foreign MNCs will be encouraged to set up in countries where they expect to receive high net profit.)
